<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">spells</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">spells</ansi> command lists spells you have learned, along with useful information
about each one.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">spells</ansi>
  To get help on a particular spell: <ansi fg="command">help spell [spellId]</ansi>
  To cast a spell: <ansi fg="command">cast [spellId]</ansi>  (or just type the spell ID directly)

<ansi fg="yellow">How spellcasting works — folds:</ansi>

Casting a spell is not instantaneous. It is a process of bifurcation: you
form a precise mental image of what you want to be true, then split that
image into two identical copies held simultaneously. Then split again.
Each doubling is called a <ansi fg="white-bold">fold</ansi>.

Different spells require different numbers of folds before they resolve.
Simple effects resolve quickly. Complex ones take longer.

When you <ansi fg="command">cast</ansi>, you begin accumulating folds each round. You cannot act
freely while doing so — your concentration is occupied. Once you have
accumulated enough folds, the spell resolves automatically.

<ansi fg="yellow">What affects casting speed:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="white-bold">Perception</ansi> — determines how many folds you can sustain per round.
  A sharper mind accumulates folds faster and finishes casting sooner.

  <ansi fg="white-bold">Spellcasting skill</ansi> — improves fold rate and your chance of successfully
  initiating a cast in the first place.

  <ansi fg="white-bold">Taking damage</ansi> — disrupts concentration. Significant hits during casting
  may cause you to lose your folds and have to start over.

<ansi fg="yellow">Discovering new spells:</ansi>

Spells are not taught by trainers. Each time you successfully cast a spell,
there is a chance a new pattern crystallizes in your mind — a spell you did
not know before. The more you cast, the more you learn.

Your <ansi fg="white-bold">spellcasting skill</ansi> determines which spells can emerge. Low-fold
spells appear early; powerful high-fold spells require significant mastery
before they reveal themselves.

<ansi fg="yellow">Conviction:</ansi>

Each spell has a <ansi fg="white-bold">conviction cost</ansi> — the sustained belief required to complete
it. You must have enough conviction to cover the full cost before you can
begin. Conviction regenerates over time.

<ansi fg="yellow">Cooldown:</ansi>

Initiating a cast uses the shared <ansi fg="white-bold">special-move</ansi> slot. You cannot bash,
kick, trip, or begin another cast until that cooldown clears. See
<ansi fg="command">help special</ansi> for details.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help cast</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help special</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cooldowns</ansi>
